  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 3,\n  \"section_title\": \"Grammar and Vocabulary (B2)\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 21,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct translation for 'It was said that he had finished his project'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) He has completed his work.\",\n        \"B) His work was completed.\",\n        \"C) It is said that he had finished the project.\",\n        \"D) The project was done by him.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 22,\n      \"question\": \"Which sentence uses the passive voice correctly?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) The book was written by Jane Austen.\",\n        \"B) She wrote a new novel last week.\",\n        \"C) The cake is baked every Saturday morning.\",\n        \"D) They have been listened to the music.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 23,\n      \"question\": \"Choose the appropriate conditional form to express 'If I were richer, I would buy a new car'.\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Present Simple\",\n        \"B) Past Perfect\",\n        \"C) Present Continuous\",\n        \"D) Future Perfect\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 24,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a correct use of 'although' in a sentence?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Although it was raining, I went for a walk.\",\n        \"B) Although he is tired, he stayed up late.\",\n        \"C) Despite she had finished her work, she continued working.\",\n        \"D) Because it was raining, I went for a walk.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 25,\n      \"question\": \"Which collocation is correct?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) take charge of\",\n        \"B) handle responsibility for\",\n        \"C) give command to\",\n        \"D) manage authority on\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 26,\n      \"question\": \"Which dependent prepositional phrase correctly modifies the main clause?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) When I arrived at the station, they were still playing.\",\n        \"B) Because it was raining he decided to stay home.\",\n        \"C) As soon as she finished her work, she went for a walk.\",\n        \"D) After the meeting ended, everyone left.\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 27,\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following expressions is a discourse marker used to introduce a reason?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Therefore\",\n        \"B) However\",\n        \"C) Moreover\",\n        \"D) As a result\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 28,\n      \"question\": \"Which word best completes the sentence: 'She often finds herself \\_\\_\\_ her thoughts.'?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) lost\",\n        \"B) getting lost\",\n        \"C) being lost\",\n        \"D) to lose\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 29,\n      \"question\": \"Choose the correct verb tense for 'It is stated that they will have finished their project by next week.'\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Present Simple\",\n        \"B) Past Perfect\",\n        \"C) Future Continuous\",\n        \"D) Present Perfect\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 30,\n      \"question\": \"Which phrase is correctly used to express a cause-effect relationship?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A) Due to\",\n        \"B) As if\",\n        \"C) In spite of\",\n        \"D) Despite\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"A\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe solution is:\n\n**1. Which word best completes the sentence: 'She often finds